# React Coding Style

**File organization** for this repo lives in `21-file-organization.mdc` (colocate → lift; kebab-case folders; per-component `skeleton.tsx`). Use that model — not a hybrid `sections/` layout.

## File Extensions

- `.tsx` for any file containing JSX
- `.ts` for pure logic, custom hooks without JSX, type definitions
- `.test.tsx` / `.test.ts` mirroring the source file

## Naming

- Component **symbols**: `PascalCase`; **files/folders**: `kebab-case` (`user-card.tsx` / `user-card/index.tsx` export `UserCard`)
- Custom hooks: `useCamelCase` symbol, kebab-case file (`use-debounce.ts`)
- Context: `<Domain>Context`, `<Domain>Provider`, `use<Domain>`
- Event handlers: `handleClick` inside; prop `onClick`
- Boolean props: `isLoading`, `hasError`, `canSubmit`

## Component Shape

```tsx
type Props = {
  user: User
  onSelect: (id: string) => void
}

export function UserCard({ user, onSelect }: Props) {
  return (
    <button type="button" onClick={() => onSelect(user.id)}>
      {user.name}
    </button>
  )
}
```

- Prefer `type Props = {}` for closed prop shapes
- Always destructure props in the parameter list
- Default export only for Next.js `page.tsx` / `layout.tsx` / `route.ts` entry files; prefer named exports elsewhere

## JSX

- Self-close tags with no children
- Use fragments when no DOM wrapper is needed
- Extract multi-line conditional logic above the return

## Server / Client Boundary (App Router)

- Default new files to Server Components — add `"use client"` only for state, effects, refs, browser APIs, or event handlers
- `"use client"` on line 1 before imports
- Never put `"use client"` on `page.tsx` — keep the page a Server Component and extract interactive regions into Client Components
- Never import server-only modules into client files

## shadcn as UI foundation (HARD RULE)

Never invent UI primitives or one-off styled controls from raw HTML/`div` soup. Always start from shadcn:

1. Prefer an existing primitive in `components/ui/` (`Button`, `Input`, `Card`, etc.).
2. If it is missing, add it with `pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add <component>` first.
3. Build feature UI by composing and wrapping those primitives — extend via props, variants, and thin feature components, not by reimplementing the control.

Raw elements are only acceptable when no shadcn (or Base UI) primitive can express the need (e.g. a layout `div`, semantic `main`/`section`, or a GSAP animation host). Form controls, dialogs, menus, tabs, and similar interactive UI always go through shadcn.

### Field + TanStack Form

Wire labelled inputs with `Field` / `FieldLabel` / `FieldError` once those shadcn pieces are installed. Pair with TanStack Form + Zod (see `20-portfolio-stack.mdc`).

### Icon-only buttons

Wrap icon-only buttons in `Tooltip`; match `aria-label` to tooltip text; describe the action, not the icon.

### Inputs need placeholders

Every `Input` / `Textarea` sets a `placeholder` showing expected format or blank-means-something.

## Imports

- React first, then third-party, then `@/` absolute, then relative
- Type-only imports: `import type { … }`

## State

- Local first (`useState`), lift only when shared
- URL state via **nuqs** when it should be shareable/bookmarkable
- Context for low-frequency cross-cutting reads (theme)
- Server data via **tRPC** (+ TanStack Query) — not ad-hoc `useEffect` fetches

## Class Components

Forbidden in new code.
